@startuml 03-epic-breakdown
title Epic Breakdown - Stories, Dependencies, and Parallel Tracks (19 pts)

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #6B8CB8
  BackgroundColor #EEF3FA
}

rectangle "**S1 - CI/CD Standard (ADR)**\n3 pts | spike -> decision record\nBranching, targets, identity,\nsecrets, gates, rollback" as S1 #FFF8E1

rectangle "**S2 - Job Template + Pipeline**\n5 pts | reference DABs bundle,\nCI validate/deploy, dev->prod" as S2
rectangle "**S3 - Job SOP**\n2 pts | step-by-step doc,\nlinks to template" as S3

rectangle "**S4 - App Template + Pipeline**\n5 pts | app resource, grants,\nsource sync + apps deploy" as S4
rectangle "**S5 - App SOP**\n2 pts | incl. app identity\n& access model" as S5

rectangle "**S6 - Pilot Validation & Publish**\n2 pts | external team deploys\nusing docs only" as S6 #E8F5E9

rectangle "**Dependency risk (external)**\nService principal provisioning +\nCI auth (OIDC / secrets).\nIf owned by cloud/IAM team,\nsplit into its own ticket." as DEP #FFEBEE

S1 --> S2
S1 --> S4
S2 --> S3
S4 --> S5
S3 --> S6
S5 --> S6
DEP .[#B71C1C].> S2
DEP .[#B71C1C].> S4

note right of S1
  **Blocks everything.**
  Do first; approve as a team.
end note

note bottom of S6
  Track A (S2->S3) and Track B (S4->S5)
  run **in parallel** after S1 lands.
end note
@enduml
